{
  "name": "SONAM EA professor takes up key position at international nursing organisation",
  "parent_id": 203314050042021,
  "group_id": "15bdd7f6-f349-4aea-aca3-acd081c4e2bd",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T15:25:18.495Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:14:16.579Z",
  "published_at": "2026-08-12T15:14:16.566Z",
  "id": 203716683788488,
  "uuid": "597a9e96-61e7-46c7-aca6-88fa824b0a4f",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "0ca2966e-26d9-98b2-2e76-52377fa9a4fe",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "a8f4b460-25a3-9afe-8bf8-90500d2011fa",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Health services aren't getting the most out of nurses, who are often undervalued and unable to work to their full potential,\" Nursing Now's website states. \"The potential of nurses to do more varied jobs and take on more responsibility is often overlooked because of strict hierarchies and engrained ideas about what they can and cannot do.\" ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Earlier this year, Edwards was named a Fellow of the London-based ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Royal College of Midwives",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "/news/sonam-ea-professor-receives-national-midwifery-award",
                        "uuid": "e1c9cc8e-581b-53d1-9bdf-35da5659aaff",
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_blank",
                        "linktype": "story"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", in recognition of her outstanding contributions in the field of midwifery across her more than 40-year career. She has been instrumental in the launch of AKU's Bachelor of Science in Midwifery in Uganda, the first such programme in the country. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Before joining SONAM EA, she worked in the United Arab Emirates to standardise midwifery practice as part of the Abu Dhabi Government Health Authority. She is also regarded as being one of the UK's pioneering consultant midwives.  ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"I am honoured to play a key role in the Nursing Now initiative in Uganda.\" said Dr Edwards. \"As we strive to provide universal health coverage, it is crucial that nurses and midwives are empowered to play a central role in proving essential care.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "AKU has graduated nearly 2,400 nurses and midwives in Uganda, Kenya and Tanzania, many of whom hold leadership positions in hospitals, clinics, nursing schools and ministries of health. ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
